---A dynamic custom asset.
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__DynamicCustomAsset
---@field iosAppLink? string iOS deep link, for example, exampleApp://content/page.
---@field similarIds? gcp.searchads360_v23.StringList Similar IDs.
---@field formattedSalePrice? string Formatted sale price which can be any characters. If set, this attribute will be used instead of 'sale price', for example, On sale for $15,000.00.
---@field contextualKeywords? gcp.searchads360_v23.StringList Contextual keywords, for example, Sedans, 4 door sedans.
---@field itemSubtitle? string Item subtitle, for example, At your Mountain View dealership.
---@field salePrice? string Sale price which can be number followed by the alphabetic currency code, ISO 4217 standard. Use '.' as the decimal mark, for example, 15,000.00 USD. Must be less than the 'price' field.
---@field itemCategory? string Item category, for example, Sedans.
---@field imageUrl? string Image URL, for example, http://www.example.com/image.png. The image will not be uploaded as image asset.
---@field itemTitle? string Required. Item title, for example, Mid-size sedan. Required.
---@field itemAddress? string Item address which can be specified in one of the following formats. (1) City, state, code, country, for example, Mountain View, CA, USA. (2) Full address, for example, 123 Boulevard St, Mountain View, CA 94043. (3) Latitude-longitude in the DDD format, for example, 41.40338, 2.17403
---@field formattedPrice? string Formatted price which can be any characters. If set, this attribute will be used instead of 'price', for example, Starting at $20,000.00.
---@field id? string Required. ID which can be any sequence of letters and digits, and must be unique and match the values of remarketing tag, for example, sedan. Required.
---@field iosAppStoreId? string iOS app store ID. This is used to check if the user has the app installed on their device before deep linking. If this field is set, then the ios_app_link field must also be present.
---@field androidAppLink? string Android deep link, for example, android-app://com.example.android/http/example.com/gizmos?1234.
---@field id2? string ID2 which can be any sequence of letters and digits, for example, red. ID sequence (ID + ID2) must be unique.
---@field price? string Price which can be number followed by the alphabetic currency code, ISO 4217 standard. Use '.' as the decimal mark, for example, 20,000.00 USD.
---@field itemDescription? string Item description, for example, Best selling mid-size car.

