---A radius around a list of locations specified through a feed.
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__LocationGroupInfo
---@field radiusUnits? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__LocationGroupInfoRadiusUnitsEnum|string Unit of the radius. Miles and meters are supported for geo target constants. Milli miles and meters are supported for feed item sets. This is required and must be set in CREATE operations.
---@field radius? string Distance in units specifying the radius around targeted locations. This is required and must be set in CREATE operations.
---@field enableCustomerLevelLocationAssetSet? boolean Denotes that the latest customer level asset set is used for targeting. Used with radius and radius_units. Cannot be used with feed, geo target constants or feed item sets. When using asset sets, either this field or location_group_asset_sets should be specified. Both cannot be used at the same time. This can only be set in CREATE operations.
---@field geoTargetConstants? gcp.searchads360_v23.StringList Geo target constant(s) restricting the scope of the geographic area within the feed. Currently only one geo target constant is allowed.
---@field feedItemSets? gcp.searchads360_v23.StringList FeedItemSets whose FeedItems are targeted. If multiple IDs are specified, then all items that appear in at least one set are targeted. This field cannot be used with geo_target_constants. This is optional and can only be set in CREATE operations.
---@field locationGroupAssetSets? gcp.searchads360_v23.StringList AssetSets whose Assets are targeted. If multiple IDs are specified, then all items that appear in at least one set are targeted. This field cannot be used with feed, geo target constants or feed item sets. When using asset sets, either this field or enable_customer_level_location_asset_set should be specified. Both cannot be used at the same time. This can only be set in CREATE operations.

---@alias gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__LocationGroupInfoRadiusUnitsEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"UNKNOWN"|"METERS"|"MILES"|"MILLI_MILES"

