---An asset representing a mobile app.
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__MobileAppAsset
---@field appId? string Required. A string that uniquely identifies a mobile application. It should just contain the platform native id, like "com.android.ebay" for Android or "12345689" for iOS.
---@field linkText? string Required. The visible text displayed when the link is rendered in an ad. The length of this string should be between 1 and 25, inclusive.
---@field startDate? string Start date of when this asset is effective and can begin serving, in yyyy-MM-dd format.
---@field appStore? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__MobileAppAssetAppStoreEnum|string Required. The application store that distributes this specific app.
---@field endDate? string Last date of when this asset is effective and still serving, in yyyy-MM-dd format.

---@alias gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__MobileAppAssetAppStoreEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"UNKNOWN"|"APPLE_APP_STORE"|"GOOGLE_APP_STORE"

---A mobile app category criterion.
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__MobileAppCategoryInfo
---@field mobileAppCategoryConstant? string The mobile app category constant resource name.

---A mobile application criterion.
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__MobileApplicationInfo
---@field name? string Name of this mobile application.
---@field appId? string A string that uniquely identifies a mobile application to Google Ads API. The format of this string is "{platform}-{platform_native_id}", where platform is "1" for iOS apps and "2" for Android apps, and where platform_native_id is the mobile application identifier native to the corresponding platform. For iOS, this native identifier is the 9 digit string that appears at the end of an App Store URL (for example, "476943146" for "Flood-It! 2" whose App Store link is "http://itunes.apple.com/us/app/flood-it!-2/id476943146"). For Android, this native identifier is the application's package name (for example, "com.labpixies.colordrips" for "Color Drips" given Google Play link "https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.labpixies.colordrips"). A well formed app id for Google Ads API would thus be "1-476943146" for iOS and "2-com.labpixies.colordrips" for Android. This field is required and must be set in CREATE operations.

---A mobile device criterion.
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__MobileDeviceInfo
---@field mobileDeviceConstant? string The mobile device constant resource name.

