---A Proximity criterion. The geo point and radius determine what geographical area is included. The address is a description of the geo point that does not affect ad serving. There are two ways to create a proximity. First, by setting an address and radius. The geo point will be automatically computed. Second, by setting a geo point and radius. The address is an optional label that won't be validated.
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__ProximityInfo
---@field radiusUnits? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__ProximityInfoRadiusUnitsEnum|string The unit of measurement of the radius. Default is KILOMETERS.
---@field radius? number The radius of the proximity.
---@field geoPoint? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__GeoPointInfo Latitude and longitude.
---@field address? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__AddressInfo Full address.

---@alias gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__ProximityInfoRadiusUnitsEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"UNKNOWN"|"MILES"|"KILOMETERS"

