---@field shoppingProductAd? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__ShoppingProductAdInfo Details pertaining to a Shopping product ad.
---@field expandedTextAd? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__ExpandedTextAdInfo Details pertaining to an expanded text ad. Expanded text ads are deprecated. Use `ResponsiveSearchAd` instead.
---@field responsiveDisplayAd? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__ResponsiveDisplayAdInfo Details pertaining to a responsive display ad.
---@field demandGenProductAd? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__DemandGenProductAdInfo Details pertaining to a Demand Gen product ad.
---@field displayUrl? string The URL that appears in the ad description for some ad formats.
---@field shoppingComparisonListingAd? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__ShoppingComparisonListingAdInfo Details pertaining to a Shopping Comparison Listing ad.
---@field searchAds360ExpandedTextAd? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__SearchAds360ExpandedTextAdInfo Immutable. Details pertaining to an expanded text ad. Expanded text ads are deprecated. Use `SearchAds360ResponsiveSearchAd` instead.
---@field urlCustomParameters? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__CustomParameterList The list of mappings that can be used to substitute custom parameter tags in a `tracking_url_template`, `final_urls`, or `mobile_final_urls`. For mutates, use url custom parameter operations.
---@field localAd? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__LocalAdInfo Details pertaining to a local ad.
---@field searchAds360ExpandedDynamicSearchAd? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__SearchAds360ExpandedDynamicSearchAdInfo Immutable. Details pertaining to an expanded dynamic search ad.
---@field trackingUrlTemplate? string The URL template for constructing a tracking URL.
---@field syntheticContentInfo? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__SyntheticContentInfo Synthetic content info for the ad. Only ads with specific ad types are eligible for updates using the `synthetic_content_info` field. Allowed `AdType` values: * `HTML5_UPLOAD_AD` * `DYNAMIC_HTML5_AD` * `IMAGE_AD`
---@field searchAds360TextAd? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__SearchAds360TextAdInfo Immutable. Details pertaining to a text ad.
---@field finalUrls? gcp.searchads360_v23.StringList The list of possible final URLs after all cross-domain redirects for the ad.
---@field productAd? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__SearchAds360ProductAdInfo Immutable. Details pertaining to a product ad.
---@field demandGenMultiAssetAd? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__DemandGenMultiAssetAdInfo Details pertaining to a Demand Gen multi asset ad.
---@field textAd? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__TextAdInfo Immutable. Details pertaining to a text ad.
---@field hotelAd? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__HotelAdInfo Details pertaining to a hotel ad.
---@field expandedDynamicSearchAd? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__ExpandedDynamicSearchAdInfo Immutable. Details pertaining to an Expanded Dynamic Search Ad. This type of ad has its headline, final URLs, and display URL auto-generated at serving time according to domain name specific information provided by `dynamic_search_ads_setting` linked at the campaign level.
---@field resourceName? string Immutable. The resource name of the ad. Ad resource names have the form: `customers/{customer_id}/ads/{ad_id}`
---@field finalUrlSuffix? string The suffix to use when constructing a final URL.
---@field shoppingSmartAd? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__ShoppingSmartAdInfo Details pertaining to a Smart Shopping ad.
---@field finalMobileUrls? gcp.searchads360_v23.StringList The list of possible final mobile URLs after all cross-domain redirects for the ad.
---@field smartCampaignAd? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__SmartCampaignAdInfo Details pertaining to a Smart campaign ad.
---@field demandGenCarouselAd? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__DemandGenCarouselAdInfo Details pertaining to a Demand Gen carousel ad.
---@field systemManagedResourceSource? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdSystemManagedResourceSourceEnum|string Output only. If this ad is system managed, then this field will indicate the source. This field is read-only.

---@alias gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdDevicePreferenceEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"UNKNOWN"|"MOBILE"|"TABLET"|"DESKTOP"|"CONNECTED_TV"|"OTHER"

---An ad group.
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroup
---@field audienceSetting? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources_AdGroup_AudienceSetting Immutable. Setting for audience related features.
---@field targetRoas? number The target ROAS (return-on-ad-spend) for this ad group. This field lets you override the target ROAS specified in the campaign's bidding strategy, but only if the campaign is using a standard (not portfolio) `TargetRoas` strategy or a standard `MaximizeConversionValue` strategy with its `target_roas` field set. If the campaign is using a portfolio bidding strategy, this field cannot be set and attempting to do so will result in an error. For any other bidding strategies, this value is ignored. To see the actual target ROAS being used by the ad group, considering potential overrides, query the `effective_target_roas` and `effective_target_roas_source` fields.
---@field excludedParentAssetFieldTypes? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupExcludedParentAssetFieldTypesItemEnumList The asset field types that should be excluded from this ad group. Asset links with these field types will not be inherited by this ad group from the upper levels.
---@field resourceName? string Immutable. The resource name of the ad group. Ad group resource names have the form: `customers/{customer_id}/adGroups/{ad_group_id}`
---@field effectiveTargetCpcSource? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupEffectiveTargetCpcSourceEnum|string Output only. Source of the effective target CPC. This field is read-only.
---@field name? string The name of the ad group. This field is required and should not be empty when creating new ad groups. It must contain fewer than 255 UTF-8 full-width characters. It must not contain any null (code point 0x0), NL line feed (code point 0xA) or carriage return (code point 0xD) characters.
---@field labels? gcp.searchads360_v23.StringList Output only. The resource names of labels attached to this ad group.
---@field cpmBidMicros? string The maximum CPM (cost-per-thousand viewable impressions) bid.
---@field creationTime? string Output only. The timestamp when this ad_group was created. The timestamp is in the customer's time zone and in "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss" format.
---@field engineStatus? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupEngineStatusEnum|string Output only. The Engine Status for ad group.
---@field fixedCpmMicros? string The fixed amount in micros that the advertiser pays for every thousand impressions of the ad.
---@field lastModifiedTime? string Output only. The datetime when this ad group was last modified. The datetime is in the customer's time zone and in "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.ssssss" format.
---@field effectiveTargetCpaSource? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupEffectiveTargetCpaSourceEnum|string Output only. Source of the effective target CPA. This field is read-only.
---@field finalUrlSuffix? string URL template for appending params to Final URL.
---@field cpvBidMicros? string The CPV (cost-per-view) bid.
---@field status? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupStatusEnum|string The status of the ad group.
---@field primaryStatus? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupPrimaryStatusEnum|string Output only. Provides aggregated view into why an ad group is not serving or not serving optimally.
---@field adRotationMode? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupAdRotationModeEnum|string The ad rotation mode of the ad group.
---@field aiMaxAdGroupSetting? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources_AdGroup_AiMaxAdGroupSetting Settings for AI Max feature in standard search adgroups.
---@field displayCustomBidDimension? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupDisplayCustomBidDimensionEnum|string Lets advertisers specify a targeting dimension on which to place absolute bids. This is only applicable for campaigns that target only the display network and not search.
---@field languageCode? string Output only. The language of the ads and keywords in an ad group. This field is only available for Microsoft Advertising accounts. More details: https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/advertising/guides/ad-languages?view=bingads-13#adlanguage
---@field startDate? string Output only. Date when this ad group starts serving ads. By default, the ad group starts now or the ad group's start date, whichever is later. If this field is set, then the ad group starts at the beginning of the specified date in the customer's time zone. This field is only available for Microsoft Advertising and Facebook gateway accounts. Format: YYYY-MM-DD Example: 2019-03-14
---@field targetCpmMicros? string Average amount in micros that the advertiser is willing to pay for every thousand times the ad is shown.
---@field id? string Output only. The ID of the ad group.
---@field baseAdGroup? string Output only. For draft or experiment ad groups, this field is the resource name of the base ad group from which this ad group was created. If a draft or experiment ad group does not have a base ad group, then this field is null. For base ad groups, this field equals the ad group resource name. This field is read-only.
---@field percentCpcBidMicros? string The percent cpc bid amount, expressed as a fraction of the advertised price for some good or service. The valid range for the fraction is [0,1) and the value stored here is 1,000,000 * [fraction].
---@field optimizedTargetingEnabled? boolean True if optimized targeting is enabled. Optimized Targeting is the replacement for Audience Expansion.
---@field endDate? string Output only. Date when the ad group ends serving ads. By default, the ad group ends on the ad group's end date. If this field is set, then the ad group ends at the end of the specified date in the customer's time zone. This field is only available for Microsoft Advertising and Facebook gateway accounts. Format: YYYY-MM-DD Example: 2019-03-14
---@field verticalAdsFormatSetting? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources_AdGroup_VerticalAdsFormatSetting Vertical ads setting feature to enable/disable ad group format controls in search campaigns. This setting requires AiMaxAdGroupSetting to be enabled and a travel feed to be attached to the campaign.
---@field demandGenAdGroupSettings? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources_AdGroup_DemandGenAdGroupSettings Settings for Demand Gen ad groups.
---@field type? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupTypeEnum|string Immutable. The type of the ad group.
---@field effectiveLabels? gcp.searchads360_v23.StringList Output only. The resource names of effective labels attached to this ad group. An effective label is a label inherited or directly assigned to this ad group.
---@field excludedParentAssetSetTypes? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupExcludedParentAssetSetTypesItemEnumList The asset set types that should be excluded from this ad group. Asset set links with these types will not be inherited by this ad group from the upper levels. Location group types (GMB_DYNAMIC_LOCATION_GROUP, CHAIN_DYNAMIC_LOCATION_GROUP, and STATIC_LOCATION_GROUP) are child types of LOCATION_SYNC. Therefore, if LOCATION_SYNC is set for this field, all location group asset sets are not allowed to be linked to this ad group, and all Location Extension (LE) and Affiliate Location Extensions (ALE) will not be served under this ad group. Only LOCATION_SYNC is currently supported.
---@field targetingSetting? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__TargetingSetting Setting for targeting related features.
---@field effectiveTargetRoasSource? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupEffectiveTargetRoasSourceEnum|string Output only. Source of the effective target ROAS. This field is read-only.
---@field effectiveTargetRoas? number Output only. The effective target ROAS (return-on-ad-spend). This field is read-only.
---@field targetCpcMicros? string Average amount in micros that the advertiser is willing to pay for every ad click. Overrides the target CPC configured at the campaign level.
---@field effectiveTargetCpc? string Output only. The effective target CPC (cost-per-click). This field is read-only.
---@field campaign? string Immutable. The campaign to which the ad group belongs.
---@field effectiveTargetCpaMicros? string Output only. The effective target CPA (cost-per-acquisition). This field is read-only.
---@field targetCpaMicros? string The target CPA (cost-per-acquisition). If the ad group's campaign bidding strategy is TargetCpa or MaximizeConversions (with its target_cpa field set), then this field overrides the target CPA specified in the campaign's bidding strategy. Otherwise, this value is ignored.
---@field effectiveCpcBidMicros? string Output only. Value will be same as that of the CPC (cost-per-click) bid value when the bidding strategy is one of manual cpc, enhanced cpc, page one promoted or target outrank share, otherwise the value will be null.
---@field excludeDemographicExpansion? boolean When this value is true, demographics will be excluded from the types of targeting which are expanded when optimized_targeting_enabled is true. When optimized_targeting_enabled is false, this field is ignored. Default is false.
---@field targetCpvMicros? string Average amount in micros that the advertiser is willing to pay for every ad view.
---@field urlCustomParameters? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__CustomParameterList The list of mappings used to substitute custom parameter tags in a `tracking_url_template`, `final_urls`, or `mobile_final_urls`.
---@field cpcBidMicros? string The maximum CPC (cost-per-click) bid. This field is used when the ad group's effective bidding strategy is Manual CPC. This field is not applicable and will be ignored if the ad group's campaign is using a portfolio bidding strategy.
---@field trackingUrlTemplate? string The URL template for constructing a tracking URL.
---@field primaryStatusReasons? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupPrimaryStatusReasonsItemEnumList Output only. Provides reasons for why an ad group is not serving or not serving optimally.
---@field engineId? string Output only. ID of the ad group in the external engine account. This field is for non-Google Ads account only, for example, Yahoo Japan, Microsoft, Baidu etc. For Google Ads entity, use "ad_group.id" instead.

---An ad group ad.
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupAd
---@field adStrength? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupAdAdStrengthEnum|string Output only. Overall ad strength for this ad group ad.
---@field resourceName? string Immutable. The resource name of the ad. Ad group ad resource names have the form: `customers/{customer_id}/adGroupAds/{ad_group_id}~{ad_id}`
---@field effectiveLabels? gcp.searchads360_v23.StringList Output only. The resource names of effective labels attached to this ad. An effective label is a label inherited or directly assigned to this ad.
---@field policySummary? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupAdPolicySummary Output only. Policy information for the ad.
---@field adGroupAdAssetAutomationSettings? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupAdAssetAutomationSettingList Settings that control the types of asset automation. See the AssetAutomationTypeEnum documentation for the default opt in/out behavior of each type.
---@field adGroup? string Immutable. The ad group to which the ad belongs.
---@field labels? gcp.searchads360_v23.StringList Output only. The resource names of labels attached to this ad group ad.
---@field engineId? string Output only. ID of the ad in the external engine account. This field is for Search Ads 360 account only, for example, Yahoo Japan, Microsoft, Baidu etc. For non-Search Ads 360 entity, use "ad_group_ad.ad.id" instead.
---@field primaryStatusReasons? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupAdPrimaryStatusReasonsItemEnumList Output only. Provides reasons for why an ad group ad is not serving or not serving optimally.
---@field primaryStatus? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupAdPrimaryStatusEnum|string Output only. Provides aggregated view into why an ad group ad is not serving or not serving optimally.
---@field lastModifiedTime? string Output only. The datetime when this ad group ad was last modified. The datetime is in the customer's time zone and in "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.ssssss" format.
---@field status? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupAdStatusEnum|string The status of the ad.
---@field ad? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__Ad Immutable. The ad.
---@field actionItems? gcp.searchads360_v23.StringList Output only. A list of recommendations to improve the ad strength. For example, a recommendation could be "Try adding a few more unique headlines or unpinning some assets.".
---@field creationTime? string Output only. The timestamp when this ad_group_ad was created. The datetime is in the customer's time zone and in "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.ssssss" format.
---@field engineStatus? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupAdEngineStatusEnum|string Output only. Additional status of the ad in the external engine account. Possible statuses (depending on the type of external account) include active, eligible, pending review, etc.

---@alias gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__AdGroupAdAdStrengthEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"UNKNOWN"|"PENDING"|"NO_ADS"|"POOR"|"AVERAGE"|"GOOD"|"EXCELLENT"

