---A currency constant.
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__CurrencyConstant
---@field name? string Output only. Full English name of the currency.
---@field symbol? string Output only. Standard symbol for describing this currency, for example, '$' for US Dollars.
---@field billableUnitMicros? string Output only. The billable unit for this currency. Billed amounts should be multiples of this value.
---@field resourceName? string Output only. The resource name of the currency constant. Currency constant resource names have the form: `currencyConstants/{code}`
---@field code? string Output only. ISO 4217 three-letter currency code, for example, "USD"

---A custom audience. This is a list of users by interest. The unique key of a custom audience consists of the following fields: name. Violating the unique key constraint produces error: CustomAudienceError.NAME_ALREADY_USED
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__CustomAudience
---@field type? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__CustomAudienceTypeEnum|string Type of the custom audience. ("INTEREST" OR "PURCHASE_INTENT" is not allowed for newly created custom audience but kept for existing audiences)
---@field name? string Name of the custom audience. It should be unique for all custom audiences created by a customer. This field is required for creating operations.
---@field members? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__CustomAudienceMemberList List of custom audience members that this custom audience is composed of. Members can be added during CustomAudience creation. If members are presented in UPDATE operation, existing members will be overridden.
---@field resourceName? string Immutable. The resource name of the custom audience. Custom audience resource names have the form: `customers/{customer_id}/customAudiences/{custom_audience_id}`
---@field description? string Description of this custom audience.
---@field id? string Output only. ID of the custom audience.
---@field status? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__CustomAudienceStatusEnum|string Output only. Status of this custom audience. Indicates whether the custom audience is enabled or removed.

---A member of custom audience. A member can be a KEYWORD, URL, PLACE_CATEGORY or APP. It can only be created or removed but not changed.
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__CustomAudienceMember
---@field url? string An HTTP URL, protocol-included — at most 2048 characters, which includes contents users have interests in.
---@field placeCategory? string A place type described by a place category users visit.
---@field keyword? string A keyword or keyword phrase — at most 10 words and 80 characters. Languages with double-width characters such as Chinese, Japanese, or Korean, are allowed 40 characters, which describes the user's interests or actions.
---@field app? string A package name of Android apps which users installed such as com.google.example.
---@field memberType? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__CustomAudienceMemberMemberTypeEnum|string The type of custom audience member, KEYWORD, URL, PLACE_CATEGORY or APP.

---@alias gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__CustomAudienceMemberList gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__CustomAudienceMember[]

---@alias gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__CustomAudienceMemberMemberTypeEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"UNKNOWN"|"KEYWORD"|"URL"|"PLACE_CATEGORY"|"APP"

---@alias gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__CustomAudienceStatusEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"UNKNOWN"|"ENABLED"|"REMOVED"

---@alias gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__CustomAudienceTypeEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"UNKNOWN"|"AUTO"|"INTEREST"|"PURCHASE_INTENT"|"SEARCH"

---A custom column. See Search Ads 360 custom column at https://support.google.com/sa360/answer/9633916
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__CustomColumn
