---Shopping performance view. Provides Shopping campaign and Performance Max campaign statistics aggregated at several product dimension levels. Product dimension values from Merchant Center such as brand, category, custom attributes, product condition, and product type will reflect the state of each dimension as of the date and time when the corresponding event was recorded. The number of impressions and clicks that `shopping_performance_view` returns stats for may be different from campaign reports. `shopping_performance_view` shows impressions and clicks on products appearing in ads, while campaign reports show impressions and clicks on the ads themselves. Depending on the format, an ad can show from zero to several products, so the numbers may not match. In Search Ads 360 UI, you can query impressions and clicks of products appearing in ads by selecting a column from "Product attributes" in the report editor. For example, selecting the "Brand" column is equivalent to selecting `segments.product_brand`.
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__ShoppingPerformanceView
---@field resourceName? string Output only. The resource name of the Shopping performance view. Shopping performance view resource names have the form: `customers/{customer_id}/shoppingPerformanceView`

---A shopping product from Google Merchant Center that can be advertised by campaigns. The resource returns currently existing products from Google Merchant Center accounts linked with the customer. A campaign includes a product by specifying its merchant id (or, if available, the Multi Client Account id of the merchant) in the `ShoppingSetting`, and can limit the inclusion to products having a specified feed label. Standard Shopping campaigns can also limit the inclusion through a `campaign_criterion.listing_scope`. Queries to this resource specify a scope: * Account: - Filters on campaigns or ad groups are not specified. - All products from the linked Google Merchant Center accounts are returned. - Metrics and some fields (see the per-field documentation) are aggregated across all Shopping and Performance Max campaigns that include a product. * Campaign: - An equality filter on `campaign` is specified. Supported campaign types are Shopping, Performance Max, Demand Gen, Video, App. - Only products that are included by the specified campaign are returned. - Metrics and some fields (see the per-field documentation) are restricted to the specified campaign. - Only the following metrics are supported for Demand Gen, Video, App campaigns: impressions, clicks, ctr. * Ad group: - An equality filter on `ad_group` and `campaign` is specified. Supported campaign types are Shopping, Demand Gen, Video, App. - Only products that are included by the specified campaign are returned. - Metrics and some fields (see the per-field documentation) are restricted to the specified ad group. - Only the following metrics are supported for Demand Gen, Video, App campaigns: impressions, clicks, ctr. Note that segmentation by date segments is not permitted and will return UNSUPPORTED_DATE_SEGMENTATION error. On the other hand, filtering on date segments is allowed.
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__ShoppingProduct
---@field availability? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__ShoppingProductAvailabilityEnum Output only. The availability of the product as provided by the merchant.
---@field productTypeLevel4? string Output only. The product type level 4 as provided by the merchant.
---@field brand? string Output only. The brand of the product as provided by the merchant.
---@field languageCode? string Output only. The language code as provided by the merchant, in BCP 47 format.
---@field multiClientAccountId? string Output only. The id of the Multi Client Account of the merchant, if present.
---@field customAttribute3? string Output only. The custom attribute 3 of the product as provided by the merchant.
---@field categoryLevel3? string Output only. The category level 3 of the product.
---@field productTypeLevel3? string Output only. The product type level 3 as provided by the merchant.
---@field currencyCode? string Output only. The currency code as provided by the merchant, in ISO 4217 format.
---@field customAttribute2? string Output only. The custom attribute 2 of the product as provided by the merchant.
---@field issues? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources_ShoppingProduct_ProductIssueList Output only. The list of issues affecting whether the product can show in ads. The value of this field is restricted to the scope specified in the query, see the documentation of the resource. This field can take up to 24 hours to update. This field is not supported for App campaigns.
---@field condition? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__ShoppingProductConditionEnum Output only. The condition of the product as provided by the merchant.
---@field itemId? string Output only. The item id of the product as provided by the merchant.
---@field productTypeLevel5? string Output only. The product type level 5 as provided by the merchant.
---@field categoryLevel2? string Output only. The category level 2 of the product.
---@field title? string Output only. The title of the product as provided by the merchant.
---@field merchantCenterId? string Output only. The id of the merchant that owns the product.
---@field productTypeLevel1? string Output only. The product type level 1 as provided by the merchant.
---@field status? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__ShoppingProductStatusEnum Output only. The status that indicates whether the product can show in ads. The value of this field is restricted to the scope specified in the query, see the documentation of the resource. This field can take up to 24 hours to update. This field is not supported for App campaigns.
---@field effectiveMaxCpcMicros? string Output only. The effective maximum cost-per-click (effective max. CPC) of the product. This field is available only if the query specifies the campaign or ad group scope, and if the campaign uses manual bidding. The value is the highest bid set for the product in product groups across all enabled ad groups. It represents the most you're willing to pay for a click on the product. This field can take up to 24 hours to update.
---@field adGroup? string Output only. An ad group of a campaign that includes the product. This field is selectable only in the ad group scope, which requires an equality filter on `campaign` and `ad_group`.
---@field productImageUri? string Output only. The URI of the product image as provided by the merchant.
---@field categoryLevel4? string Output only. The category level 4 of the product.
---@field channelExclusivity? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__ShoppingProductChannelExclusivityEnum Output only. The channel exclusivity of the product as provided by the merchant.
---@field customAttribute0? string Output only. The custom attribute 0 of the product as provided by the merchant.
---@field channel? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__ShoppingProductChannelEnum Output only. The product channel describing the locality of the product.
---@field productTypeLevel2? string Output only. The product type level 2 as provided by the merchant.
---@field targetCountries? gcp.searchads360_v23.StringList Output only. Upper-case two-letter ISO 3166-1 code of the regions where the product is intended to be shown in ads.
---@field feedLabel? string Output only. The product feed label as provided by the merchant.
---@field campaign? string Output only. A campaign that includes the product. This field is selectable only in the campaign scope, which requires an equality filter on `campaign`.
---@field customAttribute1? string Output only. The custom attribute 1 of the product as provided by the merchant.
---@field customAttribute4? string Output only. The custom attribute 4 of the product as provided by the merchant.
---@field priceMicros? string Output only. The price of the product in micros as provided by the merchant, in the currency specified in `currency_code` (e.g. $2.97 is reported as 2970000).
---@field categoryLevel1? string Output only. The category level 1 of the product.
---@field categoryLevel5? string Output only. The category level 5 of the product.
---@field resourceName? string Output only. The resource name of the shopping product. Shopping product resource names have the form: `customers/{customer_id}/shoppingProducts/{merchant_center_id}~{channel}~{language_code}~{feed_label}~{item_id}`

---@alias gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Resources__ShoppingProductAvailabilityEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"UNKNOWN"|"IN_STOCK"|"OUT_OF_STOCK"|"PREORDER"

