---A conversion adjustment.
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Services__ConversionAdjustment
---@field userAgent? string The user agent to enhance the original conversion. This can be found in your user's HTTP request header when they convert on your web page. Example, "Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 12_2 like Mac OS X)". User agent can only be specified in enhancements with user identifiers.
---@field restatementValue? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Services__RestatementValue Information needed to restate the conversion's value. Required for restatements. Should not be supplied for retractions. An error will be returned if provided for a retraction. NOTE: If you want to upload a second restatement with a different adjusted value, it must have a new, more recent, adjustment occurrence time. Otherwise, it will be treated as a duplicate of the previous restatement and ignored.
---@field userIdentifiers? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Common__UserIdentifierList The user identifiers to enhance the original conversion. ConversionAdjustmentUploadService only accepts user identifiers in enhancements. The maximum number of user identifiers for each enhancement is 5.
---@field conversionAction? string Resource name of the conversion action associated with this conversion adjustment. Note: Although this resource name consists of a customer id and a conversion action id, validation will ignore the customer id and use the conversion action id as the sole identifier of the conversion action.
---@field adjustmentDateTime? string The date time at which the adjustment occurred. Must be after the conversion_date_time. The timezone must be specified. The format is "yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm:ss+|-hh:mm", for example, "2019-01-01 12:32:45-08:00".
---@field gclidDateTimePair? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Services__GclidDateTimePair For adjustments, uniquely identifies a conversion that was reported without an order ID specified. If the adjustment_type is ENHANCEMENT, this value is optional but may be set in addition to the order_id.
---@field orderId? string The order ID of the conversion to be adjusted. If the conversion was reported with an order ID specified, that order ID must be used as the identifier here. The order ID is required for enhancements.
---@field adjustmentType? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Services__ConversionAdjustmentAdjustmentTypeEnum|string The adjustment type.

---@alias gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Services__ConversionAdjustmentAdjustmentTypeEnum "UNSPECIFIED"|"UNKNOWN"|"RETRACTION"|"RESTATEMENT"|"ENHANCEMENT"

---@alias gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Services__ConversionAdjustmentList gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Services__ConversionAdjustment[]

