---A product being planned for reach.
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Services__PlannedProduct
---@field advancedProductTargeting? gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Services__AdvancedProductTargeting Targeting settings for the selected product. To list the available targeting for each product use ReachPlanService.ListPlannableProducts.
---@field budgetMicros? string Required. Maximum budget allocation in micros for the selected product. The value is specified in the selected planning currency_code. For example: 1 000 000$ = 1 000 000 000 000 micros.
---@field plannableProductCode? string Required. Selected product for planning. The code associated with the ad product (for example: Trueview, Bumper). To list the available plannable product codes use ReachPlanService.ListPlannableProducts.
---@field conversionRate? number Conversion rate as a decimal between 0 and 1, exclusive. For example: if 2% of ad interactions are expected to lead to conversions, conversion_rate should be 0.02. This field is required for DEMAND_GEN plannable products. It is not supported for other plannable products.

---Forecasted traffic metrics for a planned product.
---@class gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Services__PlannedProductForecast
---@field conversions? number The number of conversions. This metric is only available for DEMAND_GEN plannable products. See https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/2375431 for more information on conversions.
---@field onTargetReach? string Number of unique people reached that exactly matches the Targeting. Note that a minimum number of unique people must be reached in order for data to be reported. If the minimum number is not met, the on_target_reach value will be rounded to 0.
---@field trueviewViews? string Number of ad views forecasted for the specified product and targeting. A TrueView View is counted when a viewer views a larger portion or the entirety of an ad beyond an impression. See https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/2375431 for more information on TrueView Views.
---@field totalCoviewReach? string Number of unique people reached including co-viewers. This includes people that may fall outside the specified Targeting.
---@field totalImpressions? string Total number of ad impressions. This includes impressions that may fall outside the specified Targeting, due to insufficient information on signed-in users.
---@field averageFrequency? number The number of times per selected time unit a user will see an ad, averaged over the number of time units in the forecast length. This field will only be populated for a Target Frequency campaign. See https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/12400225 for more information about Target Frequency campaigns.
---@field onTargetImpressions? string Number of ad impressions that exactly matches the Targeting.
---@field totalReach? string Number of unique people reached. This includes people that may fall outside the specified Targeting. Note that a minimum number of unique people must be reached in order for data to be reported. If the minimum number is not met, the total_reach value will be rounded to 0.
---@field totalCoviewImpressions? string Total number of ad impressions including co-viewers. This includes impressions that may fall outside the specified Targeting, due to insufficient information on signed-in users.
---@field onTargetCoviewImpressions? string Number of ad impressions that exactly matches the Targeting including co-viewers.
---@field viewableImpressions? string Number of times the ad's impressions were considered viewable. See https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/7029393 for more information about what makes an ad viewable and how viewability is measured.
---@field onTargetCoviewReach? string Number of unique people reached that exactly matches the Targeting including co-viewers.

---@alias gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Services__PlannedProductList gcp.searchads360_v23.GoogleAdsSearchads360V23Services__PlannedProduct[]

